            <title>[LU-20922] sanityn test_45j: striped dir mrename fails (err=255)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20922</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;review-dne-part-5, RHEL 9.7 ldiskfs, build 133242 (change 62389 PS18, session 54f564e0-3025-4c75-9425-cb05cd0e3182, test_set 0c589a3b-8011-4b3e-8473-5f155980c121):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanityn test_45j: @@@@@@ FAIL: iter=76 : striped dir -i1 -c2 -H crush  /mnt/lustre2/d45j.sanityn ldlm.namespaces.mdt-lustre-MDT0001_UUID.lock_count=3 ldlm.namespaces.mdt-lustre-MDT0002_UUID.lock_count=1 mrename f45j.sanityn-2 to f45j.sanityn failed (err=255);&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_45j repeatedly renames files across a crush-hashed striped&lt;br/&gt;
directory under DNE and checks per-MDT lock counts; this iteration's&lt;br/&gt;
mrename returned err=255. The same failure signature (iter=N :&lt;br/&gt;
striped dir ... mrename fNj.sanityn-N to fNj.sanityn failed (err=N))&lt;br/&gt;
recurred on an unrelated change, 65511 PS4, review-dne-part-5, on&lt;br/&gt;
2026-10-01 (session 7cb70dd8-4e2c-4c20-8d16-3d84c9dd39a7). &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20254" title="sanityn test_45j: mkdir /mnt/lustre2/d45j.sanityn failed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20254"&gt;LU-20254&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
covers a different test_45j failure mode (mkdir failing) and does not&lt;br/&gt;
fit this error. Change 62389's patchset 18 does not touch&lt;br/&gt;
lustre/tests/sanityn.sh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-62389-ps18-48c09b609deb on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/62389" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/62389&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
